TI  - Policy protocols for building a partnership between the public and marine scientists:: The ocean sequestration of CO2 experiment
T2  - GREENHOUSE GAS CONTROL TECHNOLOGIES
LA  - English
CP  - 4th International Conference on Greenhouse Gas Control Technologies (GHGT-4)
AB  - This paper presents policy protocols that address the growing challenge to marine scientists from increased public scrutiny of their research, particularly when ii has the appearance of impacting the ocean environment. This shift in the political environment could possibly affect the forthcoming experiments for ocean sequestration of CO2.
   This work 1) gives insights into the conditions motivating the need for policy protocols; 2) elaborates a set of protocols that draws on the lessons from case studies of several marine scientific projects studied in great detail, i.e., deep-sea drilling, ATOC, and Ocean Fertilization; and 3) notes the difficulties inherent in "democratizing" marine science to build public trust while striving to maintain high scientific standards and avoid delays and higher costs.
   The current policy atmosphere demands a partnership between scientists and the public, with the goals of 1) establishing trust; 2) educating the public about the science and the applications: and 3) educating the scientists about the concerns of the public. This paper addresses the initial steps toward achieving these ends.
