AB  - As a highly efficient absorber, amine-based solvents are extensively utilized in the desulfurization and decarbonization industrial process from nature gas, power plant and other plants. However, during the operation of carbon capture systems using amine solutions, various heat stable salts (HSS) are observed because of solvent degradation and external impurities. In comparison to traditional purification methods such as distillation and ion exchange, electrodialysis (ED) offers distinct advantages in terms of energy consumption, environmental sustainability, efficiency, and continuous operational capability. This study introduces the research progress in amine solution purification for CO2 capture using ED. It systematically describes the purification mechanism of ED, device characteristics, and discusses key operational parameters affecting ED performance, which includes voltage, flow rate, solution composition and so on. The analysis emphasizes critical challenges including membrane fouling, stability, and polarization effects in practical ED applications, discusses further research directions, and outlines the development trends of ED in CO2 capture.
